course: dictionary
lesson: 11955
title: Carriageway: the part of the road for vehicles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A carriageway is the part of a road where vehicles drive. Read the words around it to work out what it means. «The northbound carriageway was closed after the crash, so cars had to use the other side.» Cars and crashes are on the road, and the other side is a different part of it, so a carriageway is one side of a road.
explain: «Our bus travels along a dual carriageway, with a grass strip in the middle.» Here the clues are bus, travels and the grass strip. A dual carriageway is a big road with a strip in the middle, so it must have two sides for traffic.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Never step out onto the carriageway without looking.» If you put "the part of the road where vehicles drive" in place of carriageway, the sentence still makes sense. That tells you your meaning is right.
fact: A carriageway is the part of a road that vehicles drive on.
fact: «Carriageway» is mainly used in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: A dual carriageway has two lanes each way, with a strip in the middle.
fact: «Northbound carriageway» means the side of the road where traffic travels north.
fact: Road safety tip: never step onto the carriageway. Keep to the pavement.
exercise: «Never step out onto the carriageway without looking.» What is the carriageway? | A pavement for people to walk on | A tunnel under the hills | *The part of the road that vehicles drive on | A field beside the road
exercise: What does dual carriageway mean? | A path just for bicycles | *A big road with two lanes each way and a strip in the middle | A road that only goes one way | A road beside a river
exercise: «The northbound carriageway was closed after the crash.» Which word tells you the road was blocked? | northbound | crash | after | *closed
test: «The northbound carriageway is jammed with cars on Friday evenings.» What is a carriageway? | A field of grass | A kind of horse-drawn cart | A river crossing | *One side of a big road where vehicles drive
test: What does a dual carriageway have in the middle? | A pond | A bridge | *A strip that separates the two sides | A row of shops
exam: «The carriageway was closed, so the buses were diverted.» What does carriageway most likely mean here? | A kind of bridge | *The part of the road that vehicles drive on | A carriage pulled by horses | A bus stop
